# A known bug with the SQLite engine (../RESULTS.md, finding 4; Garage issue #1571, open). Build
# ../hydo/hydo-sqlite.yaml (on hvx: hydo build hydo/hydo-sqlite.yaml --set arch=amd64). With
# metadata_fsync = true Garage runs SQLite in WAL mode with synchronous = NORMAL, so a commit is
# not synced. The power of the whole guest goes off 10 ms after the first PutObject that Garage
# acknowledged from step 10 on. objects.acked-outcome fails: the multipart upload mpu.k93 was
# acknowledged and is gone. Fingerprint fcd596d9e0a8c850 twice on hvx with the image
# ce8592a991f3bf6a.
# The image of ../hydo/hydo.yaml (LMDB) passes it. It is not in ../hydo/regressions/, because
# that image would replay it too.
#   hydo run <image> "$(tail -1 sqlite-acked-writes-lost-at-a-power-cut.schedule)"
# expect: violation      (change to ok when the bug is fixed)
disk=cut | run A=garage.put_acked@10+10:cut
